(area "secrets" :when "an API key, token or password is involved: connecting with one, or a value computed from one leaving the REPL")

(memory "internal/secrets/header" :when "the agent is about to connect a remote server that needs an API key, token or password sent in a header, or a connection just failed on authorization"
  (format nil "Remote server that needs a secret: pass the secret as a header value in load-mcp.
Key must start ~a and be listed by (secrets) .
(load-mcp :name \"acme\" :url \"…\" :headers (list (cons \"Authorization\" (secret \"~aACME_TOKEN\")))) .
- (secrets) gives alist of (key . description) ; values hidden. Only ~a-prefixed keys are visible.
- Never type the value itself into the form. Only (secret \"KEY\") carries it.
- Secret missing from (secrets) ? Say so to the user. Do not invent a key or guess one." *secrets-env-prefix* *secrets-env-prefix* *secrets-env-prefix*))

(memory "internal/secrets/taint" :when "a string computed from a secret is about to leave the REPL, a call just refused a secret-tainted value, or the user asks where a secret's value goes"
  (format nil "- (secret \"~aTOKEN\") gives value as tainted string. Prints redacted: hash-and-angle-brackets printout naming only key.
- Works in all string functions; taint flows into every result computed from it.
- Revealed only when serialized into outgoing MCP call argument or header.
- Printout typed back errors. Call (secret \"KEY\") again, or use the name you
  bound it to." *secrets-env-prefix*))
